@startuml components
' Revision (2026-10-13): accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); design only.
' Revision 2 (2026-10-12): retain one DS note and restore the closed, linked legend.
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
' Workspace revision: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); design only.
' Revision: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); class/placement predicates and scoped handoffs.
title M-DP1: dispatcher service from slice 0 (draft; not implemented)
actor "Caller process\n(person, orchestrator or optional board adapter)\ncaller UID; principal + registered key" as C
rectangle "Service UID: swarma-dispatcher" {
  component "Service daemon from slice 0\npeer-authenticated dispatch/1 socket" as DMN
  component "Shared core\nauthority, admission, effects, reconciliation" as CORE
  component "Execution supervisor\ndaemon-owned\nservice UID" as SUP
  component "Internal daemon sweep\nevery minute" as SW
  database "Dispatcher-owned persistent state\ninput/1, agent/1, run/1, keys, claims,\neffect table, journal, index, bounded logs" as DS
}
component "swarma-user-manager\nprivileged helper (root)\nowns account ledger / termination evidence" as H
component "swarma-user-launcher\nroot until GID/UID drop\nwrites start receipt" as L
component "swarma-credential-broker\nunprivileged broker service\nowns bindings, grants/revocations, leases, secrets" as B
component "curator-run narrow exec mode\nagent UID; first broker consumer\ntrusted class + local agent placement for host loop" as E
component "swarma-session-host service\nSH2+ gated; own service UID\nowns session metadata, logs, receipts, fences" as SH
component "swarma-session-runner\nSH2+ gated; agent UID\nowns PTY/app-server and lease renewal" as SR
component "Key keeper\nlater gated integration\nowns registered identity / revocation state" as K
component "Operator command\nswarma-operator; no harness sessions\nphone-first signing / terminal fallback" as O
actor "Read-only account\nswarma-observer" as R
O --> CORE : signed team/retirement/maintenance/re-grant/all-stop/recovery/export-waiver/soft-row/trusted-circle records\norigin/confirmation checks; formats unpublished
R --> DMN : dispatcher state reads; no confirmation; no mutation
C --> DMN : signed requests on dispatch/1 (all slices)
DMN --> CORE
SW --> CORE
CORE --> DS : local lock: intent/in-flight -> unlock call -> lock/fence result\natomic records; replay on startup
CORE --> H : effect.observe; user.create / user.retire / exec.stop\ndistinct durable effect IDs; own generations
CORE --> B : revocation.check at prepare/dequeue/start\neffect.observe; trusted-only bind / unbind / E-rebind replacement; attenuated leaf\nrequest intersect caller intersect dispatcher\ncaller chain retained as dependency
CORE --> SUP : execution claim; durable registration
SUP --> L : launch.start; distinct E-launch
L --> E : root receipt; drop GID/UID; shared lifecycle R-FD3\nread-only staged plan FD3; only 0-2 + FD3 to executor
E --> B : own connection; lease\ncaller dependency rechecked
SH ..> CORE : host_start / host_stop; session-scoped host admission permit\nper-start execution/controller/op claim and fence (§12)
CORE ..> SH : durable admission / receipts; fence withdrawal or reconciliation
SH ..> SR : delivery only after current-epoch registration/readiness
SR ..> SH : fresh authenticated channel
L ..> SR : dispatcher-owned admitted start; R-FD3 lifecycle
SR ..> B : later qualified consumer; own connection
CORE ..> K : one-shot registration / separate revocation\nonly after confirmed retirement
component "Read-only per-UID sampler\nleast OS-required privilege" as W
component "Approved workspace executors\nchild UID; no network" as WX
component "Verification runners\nother machine; ephemeral; no secrets" as V
W --> CORE : R-WATCH samples; per-class thresholds
CORE --> H : v0 affected-account journaled exec.stop; hold/status in dispatcher
CORE ..> WX : R-TRANSFER materialize / export; workspace-transfer.puml
C ..> V : board/orchestrator-owned R-VERIFY; job/results formats unpublished
O ..> CORE : R-ALLSTOP direct act; commit hold at service admission
O ..> H : R-ALLSTOP direct root mark/range cut + operator stops; terminal path\nphone-to-helper transition gated
O ..> B : R-ALLSTOP direct lease/renewal freeze
O ..> SH : R-ALLSTOP direct delivery closure and snapshots
note bottom of CORE
  Refusal: principal/key/signature/chain/quota failures never queue.
  Capacity: initial refusal; later capability queues and rechecks at dequeue.
  Broker revocation.check: revoked/unavailable refuses; final broker checks stay mandatory.
  Recovery controls after ownership/schema/replay/authentication.
  Forward readiness after classification/confinement + complete accounting; retained unknown claims.
  Unbounded shared uncertainty closes admission; absent daemon refuses without fallback.
  Recursive orchestrator provisioning refused until requester-signed bootstrap is qualified.
  Unknown/contradictory observations keep records pending:
  never relaunch, release capacity or declare cleanup successful.
  Retirement: every blob/result durable outside deletion or per-act waiver before helper retiring/home deletion.
  Quiesce, declared-key cleanup; explicit operator retention only.
  Ordinary provision failure: unbind if bound, retire if created; confirm cleanup.
  Standing: no expiry/lifetime quota; sweep never expires it.
  Standing executions: no max_runtime quota or deadline; sweep never stops them for runtime.
  Ordinary executions: default 4 h, maximum 12 h; runtime expiry still stops (§§3.5, 7.2).
  R-OPERATOR: swarma-operator never hosts harness sessions; operator authority stays there.
  Signed operator records: operator device key on phone + biometric/content confirmation, or terminal password/content confirmation.
  Every operator act/record from agent sessions refuses; command/signature formats unpublished (§§3.2, 16).
  swarma-observer reads dispatcher state without confirmation; no mutation authority.
  Widening acts include export waiver, soft-row acceptance, all-stop recovery and trusted-circle admission.
  Each needs authentication and exact-content confirmation; all operator acts refuse agent-session origin.
  Standing retirement/re-creation only with operator-signed record.
  Operator-signed team/1 bring-up is specified-but-unpublished (§5.5).
  Root caller request ID is correlation, not a shared receiver key.
end note
note right of SH
  SH2+ disabled until lifecycle authorisation, host_start/host_stop and permit authentication, crash ordering,
  receipts, fences and ownership handoff are published/qualified.
  Dispatcher alone invokes the root launcher; host has no root start authority.
  Runner opens a fresh host channel; current-epoch registration/readiness before delivery.
  Owner consent gates successors; one-start replay grants none.
  Same session/op replay returns one successor; previous claim must be absent.
  Host stop stays dispatcher -> helper E-stop; host-requested, no start authority.
  Host owns output/queued-input/evidence budgets per producer and in aggregate (§§6, 9, 12-13).
  Charge before durable acceptance; retained debt survives replacement/retirement until safe disposition.
  Bound buffers/refusal; producer output cannot consume hard control/journal reserve.
  Preserve supervisor output bound; admission refuses without reserve; custody/formats open (question 5).
end note
note right of E
  §5.3 intake / Decision 0021 amendment and credential qualification
  gate activation. Caller composes; executor verifies/executes only.
  Orchestrator composes children under its own agent account/home config (§5.2).
  Child profile/environment access and grant constraints remain open (§16).
  Executor CLI/plan schema are unspecified in spec §5.3.
end note
note right of K
  Standing identity revocation is operator-only with a signed record.
  Keeper API/process UID is unspecified in spec §14.
  Broker service UID spelling is unspecified in spec §3.1.
end note
note bottom of DS
  R-LOCK wait graph: state lock -> local state I/O; unlocked workers -> helper/launcher/broker.
  Old daemon-instance writers fenced; R-FATE table is user-manager §7.
  R-GEN restore: external fence, independent coverage, reverse inventory and orphan obligations.
  R-REBIND: authorised current chains, same random 128-bit account generation, never wider.
  R-NETBIND: machine-owned policy pinned at prepare; caller text not authority.
  R-TIME: durable watermark; trusted time + monotonic lifetime gates expiry destruction.
  R-SVC-EGRESS: dispatcher/host deny-all under v1 service rows; DNS separately qualified.
  R-WORKPLACE: separate gated allocation; service-owned swarma-rb-exec, never workplace UID.
  R-TRANSFER: child-UID materialize/export; exact archive/mode-aware immutable B manifest checks.
  Each physical materialize/work/export has distinct execution evidence; bounded expiry cleanup consent.
  Refusal immutable; current-authority bounded repair/per-act waiver; security holds stay; standing discard off.
  Complete-content custody outside deletion; current-authenticated original-caller retrieval/release.
  Independent repository-B import manifest recomputation; workspace-transfer.puml (§5.2).
  Task resources read-only next to workspace; plan covers digests; data, never instructions.
  Worker requests more by letter/outcome and never fetches.
  DRAFT workspace-result/1 schema in schemas/workspace-result-1.schema.json; blobs, never inline content.
  No dispatcher repository; board import/candidate/review/integration unpublished.
  Review: positive role/class/placement admission; membership is insufficient (§3.6).
  Exact-C inert diffs/blobs outside discovery roots; tree entry needs qualified strict adapter.
  No candidate control-surface adoption; verdict is not control-context admission.
  Integration-baseline cumulative sensitive/provenance obligations; fresh exact-C acknowledgements.
  Optional reviewer policies off/unchosen; external-effect performer open for stage T (questions 30, 32).
  R-UNTRUSTED/R-CEILINGS: recorded class and qualified host matrix, no OS-name exclusion.
  Slice 0/helper v0 refuse untrusted; workplace untrusted unless operator-admitted to trusted circle, no subscription binding/lease.
  Trusted-circle admission enables donor-side opt-ins only; workplace host boundaries stay.
  R-NET-TOOL/R-RANGE-DENY: workplace zero egress, trusted provider-only proxies; static range rule from v0.
  Web default-off; explicit per-identity trusted-circle opt-in only; host boundaries stay.
  No direct/external-http-proxy binding for any platform-host account.
  N15 (2026-10-13): one listener per account_generation, bound to profile_ref; own port only.
  served_policy_digest and service_generation evidence; contract owned by N15.
  R-EXEC/R-VERIFY: protected machine selection + immutable body pin; full invocation/input qualification.
  Worker-code execution/builds/tests are off-host; out-of-bound selection or drift refuses.
  R-STANDING: trusted class AND local agent placement for host loops; circle membership supplies neither.
  Remote placements stay workplaces with donor loops; surface drift refuses launch/restart/resume.
  R-SOCKETS/R-SHARED: declared socket set only; no shared services on untrusted hosts.
  R-WATCH v0/S0a: affected-account journaled stop, admission hold, observer status only.
  No per-account egress-freeze or phone-alert promise; v1/S2 lifecycle open (§§7.3, 16).
  R-ALLSTOP: direct independent service cuts/stops; receiver launch/create/ingress fence before absence.
  Never-launched generations need fresh fenced absence + complete launch coverage.
  Dispatcher failure permits direct stops, but whole-act completion needs its durable part too.
  Explicit recovery only after all parts; no automatic restart (§6).
end note
